# PAM stack for `aa-headunit-kiosk@.service`'s `PAMName=aa-headunit-kiosk`
# — matches cage's own documented systemd deployment recipe
# (https://github.com/cage-kiosk/cage/wiki/Starting-Cage-on-boot-with-systemd).
# The `pam_systemd.so` line is the one that actually matters here: it
# registers a real logind session/seat for the service's process, which
# is what grants DRM device access dynamically via logind's seat ACLs —
# without it, `cage` would not have permission to become DRM master.
auth     required  pam_unix.so nullok
account  required  pam_unix.so
session  required  pam_unix.so
session  required  pam_systemd.so
